# best-effort.list - arsenal packages that MAY be absent from the Debian/Kali
# apt archives on some suites and therefore must be installed BEST-EFFORT, never
# as a hard dependency that aborts a build.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (OVA/ISO parity). The golden/OVA path (build-golden.sh)
# and the engine's own packaging/bootstrap-apt.sh install the curated arsenal
# best-effort per-package: a package with no apt candidate produces a warning and
# the build continues (the engine's runtime arsenal-check self-heals the residual
# via src/runner/arsenal-check.ts). live-build, by contrast, installs a
# config/package-lists/*.list.chroot ALL-OR-NOTHING, so a single name that apt
# cannot locate aborts the WHOLE ISO build with
# "E: Unable to locate package <name>", even though the identical OVA build only
# warns. That asymmetry (same apt SOURCES on both paths - Debian + pinned Kali +
# vacti - but hard-fail vs best-effort install semantics) is the bug this file
# fixes: build-iso.sh keeps the hard package-list to the resolvable packages and
# installs the names below via config/hooks/normal/0330-vpn-besteffort.hook.chroot
# with the same warn-and-continue semantics the OVA uses.
#
# These remain in the generated arsenal list (the OVA arsenal.list and the ISO's
# generated vacti-core list, derived from the engine manifest by
# gen-live-build-list.sh); this file only marks which of them must not hard-fail
# the ISO. It is a distro-OWNED install-policy file, independent of where the
# package names originate.
#
# One package per line. Comments (#...) and blank lines are ignored.
#
# globalprotect-openconnect: gpclient's real GlobalProtect portal pre-auth flow.
# Not packaged in Debian 13 trixie NOR in the pinned Kali rolling archive (only
# gp-saml-gui exists there, and openconnect already covers the GlobalProtect
# tunnel via `openconnect --protocol=gp`). Verified absent via apt-cache policy
# on a debian:trixie chroot with the pinned Kali source active. The engine's
# bootstrap-apt.sh documents it as "absent from some Debian suites" and installs
# it best-effort; the runtime arsenal-check maps gpclient -> this package for
# post-boot self-heal where an archive does carry it.
globalprotect-openconnect
